<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elena Glinskaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1508–<a href="/years/1538">1538</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elena Glinskaya was the second wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasily-iii-of-moscow">Vasily III of Moscow</a> and the mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a>, for whom she ruled as regent from 1533 until her death in 1538. Of a Lithuanian princely family that had fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, she imprisoned rival claimants, including her husband's brothers, and carried out a reform unifying the Muscovite coinage in 1535. Her sudden death, possibly by poisoning, opened years of boyar rivalry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elena-glinskaya.jpg" alt="Elena Glinskaya" width="320" height="493" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sergey Nikitin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Glinskaya_reconstruction_02.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
